From ceeee3adefa08869d9e68f77b17539d621cae499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Chase <brad@unitary.foundation>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:59:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sampling): keep noise sampling state in locals
 (experiment variant)

Copy the executor RNG and every table pointer, size and destination word
pointer that packed noise sampling needs into locals before the sampling
loops, and write the RNG back before the symbols are finalized. The loops
call std::log, which the compiler must treat as clobbering executor and
plan memory, so each draw previously reloaded and stored the four RNG
words through the executor and reloaded table pointers and the carrier
word capacity.

Noise-site activation now lives in one force-inlined member of a private
context struct shared by ordinary sampling and fixed-fault assignment. It
draws outcomes from the same local RNG in the same order, so seeded
output is unchanged. PackedBitColumns gains words() and word_capacity()
accessors so the context can address bits without calling set_bit.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Sonnet) <noreply@anthropic.com>
